    "captions": [
      {
        "t": 388.7,
        "who": "",
        "text": "A suitable reactive metal, such as magnesium, reacts with dilute hydrochloric"
      },
      {
        "t": 393.29,
        "who": "",
        "text": "acid to make a salt and hydrogen."
      },
      {
        "t": 396.13,
        "who": "",
        "text": "How is that different from reacting a metal carbonate with the acid?"
      },
      {
        "t": 400.22,
        "who": "",
        "text": "A metal carbonate gives carbon dioxide instead, and there"
      },
      {
        "t": 403.59,
        "who": "",
        "text": "is water as well as the salt."
      },
      {
        "t": 406.18,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Exactly."
      },
      {
        "t": 407.28,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Magnesium plus hydrochloric acid forms magnesium chloride and hydrogen."
      },
      {
        "t": 412.29,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Calcium carbonate plus hydrochloric acid forms calcium chloride,"
      },
      {
        "t": 416.38,
        "who": "",
        "text": "water, and carbon dioxide."
      },
      {
        "t": 418.88,
        "who": "",
        "text": "The word carbonate changes the predicted products."
      },
      {
        "t": 422.53,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Bubbles alone cannot tell me which gas it is."
      },
      {
        "t": 425.51,
        "who": "",
        "text": "I need the reactants and, if appropriate, a gas test."
      },
      {
        "t": 430.02,
        "who": "",
        "text": "In a teacher-managed small-scale test, hydrogen gives a"
      },
      {
        "t": 433.46,
        "who": "",
        "text": "squeaky pop with a lit splint."
      },
      {
        "t": 435.63,
        "who": "",
        "text": "We describe the observation for the exam, not try to produce or"
      },
      {
        "t": 439.24,
        "who": "",
        "text": "collect flammable gas ourselves."
      },
      {
        "t": 441.83,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Lit splint for hydrogen."
      },
      {
        "t": 443.9,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Oxygen uses a glowing splint that relights, not the same test."
      },
      {
        "t": 448.91,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Good."
      },
      {
        "t": 449.78,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Oxygen supports combustion."
      }
    ]
