    "poster": "/reallife-videos-astra/acids-metals.jpg",
    "captions": [
      {
        "t": 612.13,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Iron placed in copper sulfate solution can deposit copper"
      },
      {
        "t": 615.51,
        "who": "",
        "text": "metal while iron sulfate forms."
      },
      {
        "t": 618.32,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Why can iron do this?"
      },
      {
        "t": 620.3,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Iron is more reactive than copper."
      },
      {
        "t": 622.75,
        "who": "",
        "text": "It displaces copper from its compound."
      },
      {
        "t": 625.34,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Copper does not do the reverse in the corresponding"
      },
      {
        "t": 628.11,
        "who": "",
        "text": "ordinary classroom comparison."
      },
      {
        "t": 630.69,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Good."
      },
      {
        "t": 631.34,
        "who": "",
        "text": "The familiar product here is iron II sulfate."
      },
      {
        "t": 634.53,
        "who": "",
        "text": "This is a chemical reaction, not filtering pre-existing copper"
      },
      {
        "t": 637.94,
        "who": "",
        "text": "particles out of a blue liquid."
      },
      {
        "t": 640.37,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Does reactivity also explain how metals are extracted from ores?"
      },
      {
        "t": 644.76,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Yes."
      },
      {
        "t": 645.81,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Reactive metals such as aluminum are commonly extracted using electrolysis."
      },
      {
        "t": 650.82,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Iron oxides can be reduced using carbon-based processes."
      },
      {
        "t": 654.7,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Importantly, carbon monoxide in the blast furnace."
      },
      {
        "t": 658.26,
        "who": "",
        "text": "That removes oxygen from the iron oxide."
      },
      {
        "t": 661.43,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Unreactive metals may occur naturally as metal, but an ore"
      },
      {
        "t": 664.93,
        "who": "",
        "text": "or rock still needs processing."
      },
      {
        "t": 667.26,
        "who": "",
        "text": "Finding gold does not mean no separation or purification is ever needed."
      }
    ]
